1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,329
A thirteen-meter ladder leans against the wall of the building and starts to slide.

2
00:00:05,279 --> 00:00:09,587
Its base moves away from the wall at five meters per second.

3
00:00:09,587 --> 00:00:14,175
Play the slide or move the time, and watch how the top comes down.

4
00:00:14,175 --> 00:00:24,029
Besides the height, the problem asks about the area of the triangle formed by the ladder, the ground and the wall, and about the angle of the ladder with the ground.

5
00:00:24,029 --> 00:00:29,215
On the height graph, the slope of the curve is the rate at which the ladder comes down.

6
00:00:29,215 --> 00:00:33,896
With Go to x equals twelve meters you reach the instant of the problem.

7
00:00:33,896 --> 00:00:38,550
The three rates stay hidden in the panel until you turn on Reveal answer.

